  "completed_deductions": [
    "Under the original polynomial LND slice and three nice coordinate hypotheses, the full good-speed ideal I is stable under partial_z and extended from the actual good-coordinate subring, without reducedness.",
    "Writing I=gJ with primitive speed row f gives g in ker(E) intersect C[good], J extended from that same subring, and q in gB with every gcd multiplicity. The exact equivalence is q in I iff sum partial_i(f_i) belongs to J. Principal I therefore gives q in I.",
    "The original speed quotient has actual presentations B/I=R[z]=R[s], with the same embedded invariant ring R=(ker E)/(a_i). The quadratic change z=c0+c1*s+qbar*s^2/2 has unit c1 and nilpotent qbar, with a finite Catalan inverse.",
    "For an actual n-variable sliced LND with n-1 nice coordinates and one quadratic coordinate, the original independent-time Jacobian gives (1+td)det(Id+tL)=1 modulo the full speed ideal. Thus q^n belongs to that ideal, and the full velocity Jacobian has characteristic polynomial lambda^n and nth power zero only in the quotient.",
    "The n=4 bound excludes quotient controls of acceleration nilpotence order at least five as exact speed quotients of the stated ambient action. It does not realize orders two through four or prove sharpness.",
    "The relative-plane theorem in Berson, van den Essen and Maubach Report9918 cannot be applied here without its zero-relative-divergence premise; in the present quotient that premise is equivalent to the unresolved q membership."
  ],
